# check: fail error[E13c]: the receiver of 'Hash' is a number written as a literal
# also: compilation failed with 1 error
# L12: a "." before a name is no decimal point - "7.Hash()" is the integer 7, a member access and a call - and E13c
# then refuses it (a number written as a literal is no method's receiver); the error is that, not a lexical one
fn main() ? {
    assert 7.Hash() == I32(7).Hash()
    x := 7.5
    assert x > 7.0
}
